From fddd63815631223a794f3474869d5685362d5017 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daeho Ro <40587651+daeho-ro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:08:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] run the uv loop directly for libwebsockets 5.1

With libwebsockets 5.1, lws_service() can return after one libuv loop
iteration, allowing ttyd to enter shutdown just after it starts listening.
Run the loop owned by ttyd until its existing signal handler stops it.

Upstream: https://github.com/tsl0922/ttyd/pull/1589
OpenWrt issue: https://github.com/openwrt/packages/issues/31418

--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -610,7 +610,7 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv) {
     uv_signal_start(&signals[i], signal_cb, sig_nums[i]);
   }
 
-  lws_service(context, 0);
+  uv_run(server->loop, UV_RUN_DEFAULT);
 
   for (int i = 0; i < sig_count; i++) {
     uv_signal_stop(&signals[i]);
